.\" Manpage for lennys-benchmark
.TH LENNYS-BENCHMARK 1 "2026-10-09" "lennys-benchmark 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lennys-benchmark \- CPU and GPU benchmark with OpenGL rendering
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lennys-benchmark
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lennys-benchmark
is a self-contained CPU and GPU benchmark for Linux.  The CPU suite runs
multi-threaded integer, FP32, FP64 and memory-bandwidth tests.  The GPU suite
opens an X11 window and renders a demanding OpenGL 4.5 scene (a procedurally
generated torus-knot model with instancing, physically based shading, six
dynamic lights, HDR, bloom and ACES tonemapping) and measures geometry and
fill throughput.
.PP
The program detects the CPU, all GPUs (integrated and discrete) and, on
hybrid systems with an NVIDIA GPU, automatically re-executes itself through
PRIME render offload so that the discrete GPU is used.
.PP
Run it without arguments for a CPU+GPU benchmark, or add
.B \-\-monitor
to sample temperatures, clocks and power draw once per second.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Benchmark selection
.TP
.BR \-\-all
Run the CPU and GPU benchmarks (default).
.TP
.BR \-\-cpu
Run only the CPU benchmark.
.TP
.BR \-\-gpu
Run only the GPU benchmark.
.TP
.BR \-\-info ", " \-i
Print the detected hardware and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-list\-gpus
List every GPU found on the system.
.TP
.BR \-\-monitor
Sample CPU and GPU temperature, clock, utilisation and power draw once per
second and print a summary at the end.
.SS Durations
.TP
.BR \-\-seconds " N"
Set the duration for both benchmarks.
.TP
.BR \-\-cpu\-seconds " N"
Duration per CPU sub-test in seconds (default 3).
.TP
.BR \-\-gpu\-seconds " N"
GPU benchmark duration in seconds (default 8).
.TP
.BR \-\-threads " N"
Number of CPU worker threads (default: all logical cores).
.TP
.BR \-\-quick
Faster, less thorough CPU test set.
.SS GPU / scene
.TP
.BR \-\-quality " N"
Tessellation preset, 1 to 4 (default 3).
.TP
.BR \-\-instances " N"
Number of instanced models, 1 to 32.
.TP
.BR \-\-width " N " \-\-height " N"
Render and window resolution (default 1600x900).
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-window
Run without a visible window.
.TP
.BR \-\-interactive
Render until the window is closed (ESC quits, SPACE pauses, W toggles
wireframe, R resets the camera).
.TP
.BR \-\-vsync
Enable vertical sync.
.TP
.BR \-\-wireframe
Draw the scene as a wireframe.
.TP
.BR \-\-screenshot " FILE"
Save a rendered frame as a PPM image.
.TP
.BR \-\-gpu\-vendor " V"
Select the GPU: \fIauto\fR, \fInvidia\fR, \fIamd\fR or \fIsystem\fR (default auto).
.SS Output
.TP
.BR \-\-json " FILE"
Also write machine readable results to FILE.
.TP
.BR \-\-seed " N"
Random seed for the CPU tests.
.TP
.BR \-\-color ", " \-\-no\-color
Force or disable ANSI colours.
.TP
.BR \-\-help ", " \-h
Show the help text.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Full one-minute benchmark with live monitoring:
.PP
.nf
    lennys-benchmark --cpu-seconds 6 --gpu-seconds 30 --monitor
.fi
.TP
Quick CPU+GPU overview:
.PP
.nf
    lennys-benchmark --seconds 5
.fi
.TP
Maximum load on the discrete GPU with JSON output:
.PP
.nf
    lennys-benchmark --gpu --quality 4 --gpu-seconds 20 --json results.json
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/bin/lennys-benchmark
The benchmark binary.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nvidia-smi (1),
.BR glxinfo (1)
.SH AUTHOR
lfisbeck650-cloud.
